Documentation should evolve alongside cloud services throughout their lifecycle. Outdated documentation can slow incident resolution and increase operational risk.

Documentation updates should occur after:

* New deployments
* Configuration changes
* Security updates
* Incident reviews
* Architecture modifications
* Service retirement

# Real-Life Example:
For example, after implementing a new virtual network topology, administrators should immediately update architecture diagrams and operational procedures.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is reducing troubleshooting time because engineers always work from current documentation.

Maintaining documentation throughout the service lifecycle supports efficient cloud operations.
